{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 320 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "e27978e085ef549f079f35b08a7651e00694f5fcd3fd1b658846e390bc14daa5" :edb/db-before-t 319 :edb/db-after-t 320 :edb/tx-data [[13194139533632 50 #inst "2026-10-04T03:15:53.957Z" 13194139533632 true] [17592186087695 1020 #edb/ref 17592186242906 13194139533632 true] [17592186087695 1020 #edb/ref 17592186242909 13194139533632 true] [17592186087696 1020 #edb/ref 17592186242899 13194139533632 true] [17592186087696 1020 #edb/ref 17592186242913 13194139533632 true] [17592186087708 1020 #edb/ref 17592186242916 13194139533632 true] [17592186242899 1017 #edb/ref 17592186242900 13194139533632 true] [17592186242899 1089 "q-170494" 13194139533632 true] [17592186242899 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533632 true] [17592186242899 1100 "Find, in radians to two decimal places, the argument of $z=9-6\\text{i}.$ \n\n**Hint**: The argument of a complex number is in the range $[0,2\\pi ).$" 13194139533632 true] [17592186242899 1113 #uuid "443ea97b-0750-5e83-b945-577ff014453b" 13194139533632 true] [17592186242899 1138 false 13194139533632 true] [17592186242899 1145 "Let's plot $z$ in the complex plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930486/assets/1bc5f38d44d9df32a7493f8d210bbc17d716d8a63316e3d730a1c4258d56fe46.png)\n\nThe complex number $z$ lies in the fourth quadrant of the complex plane. Therefore $\\frac{3\\pi }{2}<arg⁡(z)<2\\pi .$ \n\nIf $\\alpha $ is the angle that $z$ makes with the positive real axis, then\n\n$$\n\\alpha =arctan⁡(\\frac{6}{9})=arctan⁡(\\frac{2}{3})≈0.588\\,00.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =arg⁡(z)=2\\pi -0.588\\,00≈5.70\n$$\n\nto two decimal places." 13194139533632 true] [17592186242900 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242901 13194139533632 true] [17592186242900 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242902 13194139533632 true] [17592186242900 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242903 13194139533632 true] [17592186242900 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242904 13194139533632 true] [175921