loper/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930486/assets/d3b5558c0268843618c52c588ffcf1c8012189041b17d52fadd6fe74c3526700.png)\n\nThe complex number $z$ lies in the second quadrant of the complex plane. Hence $\\frac{\\pi }{2}<arg⁡(z)<\\pi .$ \n\nIf $\\alpha $ is the angle that $z$ makes with the negative real axis, then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tan⁡\\alpha  & =\\frac{8}{11} \\\\ \\alpha  & =arctan⁡(\\frac{8}{11}) \\\\  & =0.628\\text{ }796\\text{ }…\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =arg⁡(z)=\\pi -0.628\\text{ }796\\text{ }…≈2.51,\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places." 13194139533632 true] [17592186242907 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242908 13194139533632 true] [17592186242907 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533632 true] [17592186242907 1041 "field-1" 13194139533632 true] [17592186242907 1104 #edb/ref 17592186242908 13194139533632 true] [17592186242907 1110 #uuid "7d1fca77-3e7f-53e3-960f-0060bd3b8855" 13194139533632 true] [17592186242908 1034 "2.51" 13194139533632 true] [17592186242908 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533632 true] [17592186242908 1111 #uuid "700aa052-5bda-5318-a176-5ea7dfe6f9b8" 13194139533632 true] [17592186242909 1017 #edb/ref 17592186242910 13194139533632 true] [17592186242909 1089 "q-319507" 13194139533632 true] [17592186242909 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533632 true] [17592186242909 1100 "Find, **in radians**, the **exact value** of the argument of $z=-5+5\\sqrt{3}\\text{i}.$\n\n**Hint**: The argument of a complex number is in the range $[0,2\\pi ).$ \n\n$arg⁡(z)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533632 true] [17592186242909 1113 #uuid "5d6c23e8-dfa9-5cf0-bb09-7d2dc3e11620" 13194139533632 true] [17592186242909 1138 false 13194139533632 true] [17592186242909 1145 "Let's plot $z$ in the complex plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930486/assets/f466a110eda3b07b50d988de6e46a541ad85d7ff64f43a6f056ea216752fa2d9.png)\n\nThe complex number $z$ lies in the second quadrant of the complex plane. Hence $\\frac{\\pi }{2}<arg⁡(z)<\\pi .$ \n\nIf $\\alpha $ is the angle that $z$ makes with the negative real axis, then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tan⁡\\alpha  & =\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{5} \\\\ \\alpha  & =arctan⁡(\\sqrt{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =arg⁡(z)=\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{3}=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.\n$$" 13194139533632 true] [17592186242910 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242911 13194139533632 true] [17592186242910 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242912 13194139533632 true] [17592186242910 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533632 true] [17592186242910 1041 "field-1" 13194139533632 true] [17592186242910 1104 #edb/ref 17592186242912 13194139533632 true] [17592186242910 1110 #uuid "05787393-74e8-587e-8a1e-ad23ec25a881" 13194139533632 true] [17592186242911 1034 "\\frac{\\pi}{3}" 13194139533632 true] [17592186242911 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533632 true] [17592186242911 1111 #uuid "dd881fba-5af0-5c8a-8787-c82bfdcf5fc9" 13194139533632 true] [17592186242912 1034 "\\frac{2\\pi}{3}" 13194139533632 true] [17592186242912 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533632 true] [17592186242912 1111 #uuid "c2002a52-1e83-5344-b1bc-0baa7e781dbb" 13194139533632 true] [17592186242913 1017 #edb/ref 17592186242914 13194139533632 true] [17592186242913 1089 "q-319562" 13194139533632 true] [17592186242913 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533632 true] [17592186242913 1100 "Find, **in radians**, the argument of $z=8-11\\text{i}.$ Round your final answer to **two decimal places**.\n\n**Hint**: The argument of a complex number is in the range $[0,2\\pi ).$ \n\n$arg⁡(z)≈$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533632 true] [17592186242913 1113 #uuid "019c203e-8df8-505f-8a2f-32d848d7aea4" 13194139533632 true] [17592186242913 1138 false 13194139533632 true] [17592186242913 1145 "Let's plot $z$ in the complex plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930486/assets/16408e6add22c687e3d2cf865908011602bfa87878f